Message-ID: <oT32UOraJXk.wsCy7EJkgdUJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/oT32UOraJXk/m/wsCy7EJkgdUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Simple test case:

Straight plot:
ggplot(data.frame(a=1:10, b=1:5), aes(x=a, y=b)) + geom_point() +
geom_hline(aes(yintercept=3))

flipped plot:

ggplot(data.frame(a=1:10, b=1:5), aes(x=a, y=b)) + geom_point() +
geom_hline(aes(yintercept=3)) + coord_flip()

in the flipped plot the line does not extend to the whole figure as in
the un-flipped plot.
Alex

