Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/rLGBCRjoy_Y/m/uOQPZXOKNywJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Daren,

Create a data frame that indicates where each label should go:

examp <- data.frame(
  X=rnorm(20),
  Y=rnorm(20),
  fact=rep(c("a","b"),each=10)
)

corr <- ddply(examp, "fact", summarise, cor = cor(X, Y))

ggplot(examp,aes(X,Y)) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_smooth(method="lm") +
  geom_text(aes(1, 1, label = format(cor)), data = corr) +
  facet_grid(fact~.)

Hadley

