You need to use the original variogram object. And I forgot that the np stuff must be an aestetic. Here is a working example

library(gstat)
library(ggplot2)
data(meuse)
coordinates(meuse) = ~x+y
v <- variogram(log(zinc)~1, meuse)
ggplot(v, aes(x = dist, y = gamma)) +  geom_smooth(aes(weight = np / dist ^ 2)) + geom_point()

HTH,

Thierry

PS Hadley, can we write methods (S3 or S4) so that ggplot does something like the code below when v is a variogram object? In this case ggplot(v) could be sufficient information for a method. As a variogram object always uses the same variable names.

